Privacy and telemetry

Data Collection. The software may collect information about you and your use of
the software and send it to Microsoft. Microsoft may use this information to
provide services and improve our products and services. You may turn off the
telemetry as described in the repository. There are also some features in the
software that may enable you and Microsoft to collect data from users of your
applications. If you use these features, you must comply with applicable law,
including providing appropriate notices to users of your applications together
with a copy of Microsoft's privacy statement. Our privacy statement is located
at https://go.microsoft.com/fwlink/?LinkID=824704. You can learn more about data
collection and use in the help documentation and our privacy statement. Your use
of the software operates as your consent to these practices.

NFV data handling

NFV has no separate usage-telemetry uploader. Results and diagnostic files from
local runs are not automatically sent to NFV maintainers. Requested inference
sends source, intent and model context to Copilot or the selected provider.
GitHub Actions retains workflow logs and evidence artifacts, and the reviewer
publishes PR comments in the consuming repository. These services have their own
data-handling policies. Optional gh-aw OpenTelemetry export sends traces to an
operator-configured endpoint; it is not enabled by an NFV-owned collector.

Turning off telemetry and avoiding cloud collection

- Optional workflow OTLP export: clear GH_AW_DEFAULT_OTLP_ENDPOINT for the
  consuming repository. Have its administrator remove or override any applicable
  organization/enterprise default for this repository, and remove any explicitly
  configured observability.otlp endpoint. The paper benchmark also reads a
  GH_AW_DEFAULT_OTLP_ENDPOINT secret; clear that secret if using that workflow.
  With no resolved endpoint, the generated workflows skip OTLP export. Do not
  merely remove authentication headers while leaving an endpoint configured.

- Copilot CLI client telemetry: when launching the CLI directly, pass
  --disable-client-telemetry. This applies only to that CLI process, not to
  separately supervised SDK/AW CLI processes or service-side collection.

- .NET CLI telemetry: set DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1 before running tools.
  In PowerShell: $env:DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT = "1"
  In a POSIX shell: export DOTNET_CLI_TELEMETRY_OPTOUT=1
  The NFV workflow's verifier subprocess already sets this opt-out.

- To avoid Microsoft/GitHub cloud collection, do not run cloud inference or
  hosted workflows. Disable the installed NFV workflows in the consuming
  repository's Actions settings, and separately cancel active/queued runs.
  Local saved-artifact checks, such as python -m paper.smoke --timeout 60,
  require no inference. Use locally installed verifiers with the opt-out above.

These controls do not erase existing logs, artifacts, provider records or
published comments. Turning off OTLP or CLI client telemetry does not prevent
service-side processing of requests you choose to send. Do not submit secrets,
personal information or source you are not authorized to share. Before collecting
data from application users, provide the required notices and comply with
applicable law and the selected providers' terms.
